'''''Pyracantha angustifolia''''' is a species of [[shrub]] in the [[Rosaceae|rose family]] known by the common names '''narrowleaf firethorn''',<ref>{{PLANTS|id=PYAN|taxon=Pyracantha angustifolia|accessdate=16 October 2015}}</ref> '''slender firethorn''' and '''woolly firethorn'''. The flowers are white and produce small round [[pome]]s and can be orange to red in color. These fruits are [[astringent]] and bitter, making them inedible for humans, but they are a food source for birds. The leaves, fruit and seeds contain [[hydrogen cyanide]], the source of the bitter taste.<ref>[http://www.pfaf.org/database/plants.php?Pyracantha+angustifolia Plants for a Future]</ref> The stems and branches have sharp spines. This shrub is cultivated and grown in yards and gardens as an [[ornamental plant]]. It can be used to make hedges for home security. This species is native to China but has been introduced to [[North America]] and [[Australia]]. It is an [[invasive species]] in [[Hawaii]] and in other areas.<ref>[http://www.hear.org/pier/species/pyracantha_angustifolia.htm info from hear.org]</ref>

